    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I see what you're saying about the different skill sets, but it feels a bit like you're making a distinction that isn't quite clear. You mention \"natural storytelling\" and \"audience engagement\" for James, but you don't really address why a top-tier lawyer like Marcus might lack that \"command\" you're looking for. \n\nTo be blunt, when you talk about \"executive presence\" and \"cultural fit,\" are you implying that certain leadership styles or ways of presenting are inherently more suited to certain backgrounds? I'm trying to understand if your assessment of \"gravitas\" is tied to specific professional pedigrees, or if there's a more subtle distinction in how these candidates would be perceived by a traditional board.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
