      "content": "I think I may have inadvertently hinted at an implicit bias towards certain professional backgrounds being more suitable for executive presence. In reality, a top-tier lawyer like Marcus Washington could still have the necessary gravitas to command a boardroom. The key factors would be not his background, but rather how he has developed his communication skills and ability to connect with his audience through experience and personal growth.\n\nWhile James Whitmont's consulting background undoubtedly provided opportunities to hone his presentation skills, Marcus Washington may have developed similar skills through his work on high-stakes negotiations, wherein clear and effective communication is paramount. Ultimately, a more nuanced assessment would look at the individual's ability to convey confidence, authority, and value without relying on their professional pedigree.",
